<title>USA: Calif. Treasurer says floods will not hurt ratings.</title>
<headline>Calif. Treasurer says floods will not hurt ratings.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>California state Treasurer Matt Fong said on Wednesday recent flooding would have no impact on the state's credit standing.</p>
<p>&quot;They've had no impact on our ratings because the majority of the dollars coming in are coming in from the federal side,&quot; Fong said in a conference call with reporters. &quot;The rating agencies were satisfied that the floods had no impact on us.&quot;</p>
<p>Fong spoke to reporters from New York, where he was meeting with major credit rating agencies. Damage estimates from the devastating New Year floods in central and northern California have surpassed $1.5 billion, state officials said.</p>
